agent: opus-optics
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/fuse-affine-preview
worktree: ../okay-wt-affine
spec: specs/optics.md (stage 11)

why: filed at the end of stage 10, and the operator said do it. An
  affine's `preview` IS emittable — `if (s.f.isDefined) Some(...) else
  None` — and okay-codec's JSON paths are affines, which is most of
  the reading this library does through an optic.

what: `emitPreview`, which unlike `emitGet` knows what to do with
  absence. Previewing `some` on an `Option` IS the Option, a lens
  step is the projection, and a `some` step in the middle is the
  test. `get` still refuses a prism, because an absent focus is not a
  value and that has not changed.

measure: the affine preview against the hand-written
  `p.address.map(_.zip)`, matched.
